# Real-World API Security Incidents

Several major organizations have experienced API-related breaches.

Examples include:

* Large telecommunications companies
* Financial institutions
* Healthcare organizations
* Technology companies

In many cases, millions of customer records were exposed because of insecure APIs.

---

# Regulations That Require API Security

Many security and privacy standards now include API protection requirements.

Some important regulations include:

| Regulation                         | Purpose                                 |
| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| PCI DSS 4.0                        | Secure payment systems and APIs         |
| GDPR                               | Protect personal data                   |
| HIPAA                              | Protect healthcare information          |
| SEC Security Rules                 | Report cybersecurity risks and breaches |
| FedRAMP                            | Secure cloud services for government    |
| Automotive Cybersecurity Standards | Protect connected vehicles              |

Organizations must ensure their APIs are secure to comply with these standards.

---

# Best Practices for API Security

Organizations should:

* Perform regular API security testing
* Use strong authentication
* Implement proper authorization
* Validate all user input
* Encrypt sensitive data
* Monitor API activity continuously
* Apply the principle of least privilege
* Fix vulnerabilities quickly

Continuous security testing is essential because APIs change frequently.



